      "Simultaneously, Lionsgate selected Lawrence to lead Suzanne Collins' dystopian franchise 'The Hunger Games' (2012) as Katniss Everdeen. Undergoing rigorous archery, combat, and wilderness training, Lawrence delivered a fierce, grounded portrayal that shattered studio conventions regarding female-led action blockbusters. The four-film series—spanning 'Catching Fire' (2013) and 'Mockingjay' Parts 1 & 2 (2014–2015)—grossed $2.97 Billion worldwide. From an initial base salary of $500,000 on the first film, Lawrence negotiated $10 Million for the sequel and $15 Million per film for the Mockingjay finale, accumulating over $40 Million in guaranteed compensation across the franchise."
