      "Lawrence reunited with Russell and Cooper for 'American Hustle' (2013), winning a BAFTA Award and earning her third Oscar nomination for her supporting turn as Rosalyn Rosenfeld. Two years later, she received a fourth Oscar nomination starring as entrepreneur Joy Mangano in 'Joy' (2015). By 2015, Forbes certified Lawrence as the highest-paid actress in the world with $52 Million in annual earnings, repeating the number-one spot in 2016 with $46 Million. During this peak commercial era, she secured a landmark $20 Million upfront salary plus 30% backend profit points for the 2016 sci-fi feature 'Passengers' opposite Chris Pratt."
